{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-158261","model_call":62,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1700"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1700"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_1389956331#1_2817468387","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1700","rank":8,"snippet":"into the global economy while its foreign trade has been further invigorated. On the 10th anniversary of <cover>China's accession to the WTO, the Chinese government issues this White Paper to give a comprehensive introduction to China's foreign trade development. I. Historic Progress in China's Foreign Trade After the founding of the People's Republic of China (PRC) in 1949, China adhered to the principle of independence and self-reliance, and gradually carried out economic and trade exchanges with foreign countries. However, hindered by the international political environment at that time and the country's planned economic system, China's foreign trade development was relatively slow. In 1978 China entered the new period of reform and opening up. Devoting major efforts to the development of foreign trade became an important approach to accelerate modernization, shake off backwardness, promote the growth of economy, and improve comprehensive national strength.\" , \"start_char\": 766.000000 , \"title\": \"China's Foreign Trade — Embassy of the People's Republic of China in the United States </cover>of America\" , \"url\": \"http://www.china-embassy.org/eng/zt/bps/t943740."},"time":10},"model_calls":62,"document_judgments":40,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
