{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-158261","model_call":64,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1700"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1700"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_216257645#3_492695224","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1700","rank":10,"snippet":"9 Economies Brazil Canada European Union Greece Guatemala Italy Japan Mexico <cover>United States from the time it acceded to the WTO in 2001 through 2019 . China has been the complainant 21 times and the respondent 44 times. Click on a bubble for more information. Complainant Respondent Multiple Participants Involved Go to a table of all disputes. Close Dispute # Complainant (s) Respondent (s) Third Parties Issues Affected Areas More details about this dispute on the WTO website. Status 1995→ ←2019 China’s Accession to the WTO Prior to joining the WTO, China had long been a member of other major international organizations, including the United Nations since 1971 and the World Bank and International Monetary Fund since 1980. 2 Nonetheless, joining the WTO proved a prolonged and challenging process for Beijing. Unlike many other economies, China’s membership was not grandfathered in, as was the case with “original members” that joined in 1995 through their membership in the WTO’s predecessor, the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT). When China acceded in December 2001, it became the 143 rd member of the WTO. China experienced explosive trade growth </cover>after joining the WTO.\" , \"start_char\": "},"time":16},"model_calls":64,"document_judgments":42,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
