{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-158261","model_call":68,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1717"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1717"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_301041849#10_684891215","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1717","rank":2,"snippet":"Bill Background of Most Favored Nation Status Advantages Disadvantages China's MFN Status Article Sources \" , \"segment\": \"Despite the friendly start to the 21st century, the two countries have since become locked in an ongoing trade dispute. Citing unfair trade practices, including intellectual theft, the Trump administration began imposing tariffs on Chinese imports in 2018. 7 ﻿ China soon introduced tariffs in retaliation. More rounds of tariffs from both sides followed throughout 2018 and 2019. 8 ﻿ In January 2020, the U.S. and China signed a \\\"Phase One\\\" trade agreement, citing multiple structural reforms to China's trade practices. As part of the agreement, <cover>China committed to purchasing an additional $200 billion in American products over 2017 levels in four sectors: manufactured goods, services, agricultural products, and energy. In turn, the United States conceded in lowering tariffs from 15% to 7.5%. 9 ﻿ Article Sources World Trade Organization. \" Principles of the Trading System .\"\" , \"start_char\": 4881.000000 , \"title\": \"Most Favored Nation </cover>Status: Advantages, Disadvantages, and Examples\" , \"url\": \"https://www.thebalance.com/most-favored-nation-status-3305840\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_301041849#11_684892622","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":7},"model_calls":68,"document_judgments":45,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
